31
00:03:05,067 --> 00:03:11,914
Hammer home that Mode, Permissions, and Isolation are three separate
dials—never conflate them!

32
00:03:11,914 --> 00:03:16,383
Plan mode is a workflow conversation, NOT a security boundary.

33
00:03:16,383 --> 00:03:21,429
And a Git worktree isolates file edits, NOT machine or network
access.

34
00:03:21,429 --> 00:03:29,574
Because Chronicle labs use private Foundry credentials in dot-env,
forbid blanket Approve-All in local checkouts.

35
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:36,699
This slide resolves one of the most common points of confusion in
advanced workshops.

36
00:03:36,699 --> 00:03:46,175
Separate three layers: the UI client window, the Harness
runtime—such as Copilot SDK, VS Code Local, Claude, or Codex—and the

37
00:03:46,175 --> 00:03:47,615
Agent Host process.

38
00:03:47,615 --> 00:03:54,165
Ask the room two check questions: Does switching from Sonnet to GPT
change the harness?

39
00:03:54,165 --> 00:03:55,595
No, only the model.

40
00:03:55,595 --> 00:03:57,025
Is Cloud a harness?

41
00:03:57,025 --> 00:03:59,510
No—Cloud is where execution runs!

42
00:03:59,510 --> 00:04:06,888
And because Agent Host owns the session in its own process, closing
a window doesn't kill the run.

43
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:15,445
Walk through the seven layers competing inside one context window
and point to the rising ten-turn bar chart.

44
00:04:15,445 --> 00:04:25,228
Every turn re-sends the accumulated conversation and tool outputs,
driving up token consumption and causing middle-of-context drift, or

45
00:04:25,228 --> 00:04:26,098
context rot.

46
00:04:26,098 --> 00:04:35,433
Connect this directly to BOTH halves of our labs: subagents keep
noisy exploration out of your main chat, and Chronicle's chunked

47
00:04:35,433 --> 00:04:39,629
summarizer turns huge transcripts into lean handoff files.

48
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:48,600
Present Research, Plan, Implement as the rhythm learners will see
their Chronicle Orchestrator execute automatically.

49
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:57,636
Research reads files and surfaces risks; Plan produces an explicit
file contract; Implement writes a focused diff and runs node

50
00:04:57,636 --> 00:04:58,703
dash-dash-test.

51
00:04:58,703 --> 00:05:03,649
Each phase passes forward a compact summary instead of raw tool
noise.

52
00:05:04,367 --> 00:05:08,753
Welcome to Part Two: Controlling Agents and Skills in Markdown.

53
00:05:08,753 --> 00:05:17,926
Slow down slightly on the next five slides—learners will author
these exact YAML frontmatter fields in Labs One and Two, so clarity

54
00:05:17,926 --> 00:05:21,217
on syntax and enforcement pays off immediately.

55
00:05:21,933 --> 00:05:27,088
Walk this table top to bottom and spotlight the rightmost column:
Guarantee!

56
00:05:27,088 --> 00:05:33,329
Instructions and Skills are model-driven—prose guides behavior, it
doesn't enforce security.

57
00:05:33,329 --> 00:05:42,402
Custom Agent tool lists enforce capability boundaries, Subagents
enforce context isolation, Hooks enforce deterministic shell checks,

58
00:05:42,402 --> 00:05:45,199
and Canvases provide shared visual state.

59
00:05:45,199 --> 00:05:48,183
Ask the room this distinction during recaps!

60
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:53,430
Break down the open Agent Skills format under dot-github slash
skills.

61
00:05:53,430 --> 00:06:01,773
Stress rule number one for Lab Two: the YAML name field must match
the parent folder name character-for-character—lowercase with

62
00:06:01,773 --> 00:06:02,294
hyphens!

63
00:06:02,294 --> 00:06:11,003
Highlight three-stage progressive disclosure on the right: metadata
costs roughly a hundred tokens at startup, the SKILL.md body loads

64
00:06:11,003 --> 00:06:17,177
only when matched, and bundled scripts execute deterministically
without bloating prompt prose.

65
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:20,819
The description field is the router trigger!

66
00:06:20,819 --> 00:06:29,497
Contrast the red anti-pattern—'Helpful test utilities'—against our
actual Lab Two skill description that names local mock servers,

67
00:06:29,497 --> 00:06:31,833
OAuth2, and Foundry client changes.

68
00:06:31,833 --> 00:06:40,717
Coach learners to test skill discovery with natural user prompts
that do NOT mention the skill's filename—if it doesn't fire, sharpen

69
00:06:40,717 --> 00:06:41,785
the description!

70
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:45,990
Walk every YAML field in chronicle-security.agent.md.

71
00:06:45,990 --> 00:06:54,813
Point out tools: read and search—omitting edit and execute creates a
true read-only auditor enforced by the harness, not polite prose.

72
00:06:54,813 --> 00:07:02,842
Explain user-invocable: false—it hides specialist workers from the
user's Chat dropdown to prevent clutter, while keeping

73
00:07:02,842 --> 00:07:11,402
